From 0811f31d07044ce601128c810e49d8c99ef1ed0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shapey Review <review@shapey.local>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:28:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] refactor(game): split GameScene into focused mixin
 modules

src/scenes/game.js had grown to 2095 lines mixing orchestration with
the inventory shop, audience polls, the online client, board motion,
attempt resolution, effects and the AI turn loop.

Extract the peripheral behaviour into prototype mixins under src/game/
(plain method sets that keep the scene as `this`, so no call site
changes):

- inventory.js   shop overlay, Star economy, streak rewards
- polls.js       Ask-the-Audience overlay
- online.js      authoritative-state reconciliation, submit queue, socket
- board-motion.js reveals, stuck-tile heal, shuffle animation
- attempts.js    picking, match/mismatch/hazard resolution, submit, score
- fx.js          sounds, destroy/dust effects, falling tiles, spawn roll
- ai-turn.js     visible AI turn loop

GameScene keeps lifecycle, layout, HUD, clocks/turn flow, board
creation and the cascade (744 lines, the orchestrator). Composition is
one Object.assign on the prototype after the class.

CI syntax checks now include src/game/*.js.

Carries the corrected Hazard behaviour from the previous commit: the
split attempts.js routes every hazard to hazardBlast() and scores the
Play Alone-only penalty through rules.hazardPenalty().
